---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/site/PageHead.astro';
import PipelineFlow from '../components/site/PipelineFlow.astro';
---

<Site
    title="Method · how a parametric trigger is computed and audited · Skaraz Data"
    description="The published method behind every Skaraz Data calculation: named data, input checks and hashes, index as worded, trigger test, payout report, audit trail."
>
    <PageHead
        label="Method"
        title="How I compute a trigger, written down so you can check it."
        lede="A calculation nobody can rerun is a matter of trust, not independence. This is the open method behind every number on this site: each report shows its sources, dataset versions and hashes."
        cta={false}
    />

    <section class="section">
        <div class="wrap">
            <PipelineFlow />
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section--tint">
        <div class="wrap rules">
            <div class="section-head reveal">
                <p class="label label--index">Rules I hold to</p>
                <h2>Seven rules, the same for every client.</h2>
            </div>
            <ol class="rl">
                <li class="reveal"><span class="num">1</span><div><h3>The wording is the specification.</h3><p class="muted">The code computes what the policy says. Where the wording is ambiguous, I write the ambiguity down and get it resolved before the season, not after an event.</p></div></li>
                <li class="reveal"><span class="num">2</span><div><h3>One code path for backtest and live.</h3><p class="muted">The index that was backtested is the index that pays. No separate script for production.</p></div></li>
                <li class="reveal"><span class="num">3</span><div><h3>Every input is checked and hashed.</h3><p class="muted">Coverage, units, gaps and known defects are tested before a value enters the index. The hash ties each figure to the exact file it came from.</p></div></li>
                <li class="reveal"><span class="num">4</span><div><h3>Fallbacks are agreed in advance.</h3><p class="muted">If the primary source is late or broken, the replacement is already named in the contract. Dataset versions are named too: CHIRPS v2 production ends after December 2026, so rainfall indices built now use CHIRPS v3.</p></div></li>
                <li class="reveal"><span class="num">5</span><div><h3>Thresholds live in the index’s own units.</h3><p class="muted">A tier is “the 1-in-10 event for this cell, as this instrument measures it”, never a claim about the atmosphere.</p></div></li>
                <li class="reveal"><span class="num">6</span><div><h3>Limits are reported, not hidden.</h3><p class="muted">Where no loss series exists, payout against loss is reported as not scored. Nothing is estimated to fill the gap.</p></div></li>
                <li class="reveal"><span class="num">7</span><div><h3>A rerun gives the same answer.</h3><p class="muted">Same inputs, same code version, same result. That is the test the audit trail exists to pass.</p></div></li>
            </ol>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <div class="wrap">
            <div class="section-head reveal">
                <p class="label label--index">See it applied</p>
                <h2>Five calculations follow this method end to end.</h2>
            </div>
            <a class="btn" href="/showcase">Open the showcase <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
    </section>
</Site>

<style>
    .rl { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; counter-reset: r; }
    .rl li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 56px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 18px; padding-block: 24px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
    .rl li > span { font: 400 1.5rem/1 var(--mono); color: var(--index); }
    .rl li div { display: grid; gap: 8px; max-width: 70ch; }
</style>
